462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 145 0 R
/T (Logistic regression is a very popular, statistically sound, probability-based classification algorithm that employs supervised learning. It was developed in the 1940s as a complement to linear regression and linear discriminant analysis methods. It has been used extensively in numerous disciplines, including the medical and social sciences fields. It differs from linear regression with one major point: its output \(response variable\) is a class as opposed to a numerical variable. That is, whereas linear regression is used to estimate a continuous numerical variable, logistic regression is used to classify a categorical variable.)
/E (Logistic regression is a very popular, statistically sound, probability-based classification algorithm that employs supervised learning. It was developed in the 1940s as a complement to linear regression and linear discriminant analysis methods. It has been used extensively in numerous disciplines, including the medical and social sciences fields. It differs from linear regression with one major point: its output \(response variable\) is a class as opposed to a numerical variable. That is, whereas linear regression is used to estimate a continuous numerical variable, logistic regression is used to classify a categorical variable.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
