464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 145 0 R
/T (Maps any input to a probability between 0 and 1, which is then mapped to a class. In predictive analytics, logistic regression models are used to develop probabilistic models between one or more explanatory/predictor variables \(which may be a mix of both continuous and categorical in nature\) and a class/response variable \(which may be binomial/binary or multinomial/multiclass\).)
/E (Maps any input to a probability between 0 and 1, which is then mapped to a class. In predictive analytics, logistic regression models are used to develop probabilistic models between one or more explanatory/predictor variables \(which may be a mix of both continuous and categorical in nature\) and a class/response variable \(which may be binomial/binary or multinomial/multiclass\).)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
